{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads","id":1189126,"title":"Homebrew Psiads","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-23T22:59:30-08:00","id":1189126,"title":"Homebrew Psiads","content":"So now that we have the rules for Psions, I know at least one of my players is going to want to play a Psiad. So this thread is a place for me to put down some ideas until the official rules come out.<br /> <br /> Idea #1) Psiads are as close to 1e as I can get. They get 2 &quot;favored&quot; Aptitudes based on pairings. (Bio/Vita, Clair/Tele, or EK/PK, TP can't ever be chosen as favored. QK can't ever be learned at all) All starting points must go to favored Aptitudes. 6xp per dot for Favored Aptitudes, 8xp per dot for non-favored Aptitudes. All Modes max out at 3 dots. Not sure the prerequisites to get to Tier 3 just yet, but when they do, the Modes of their favored Aptitudes can go to 4.<br /> <br /> #2) As #1, but you can choose TP/QK as your favored pair, but you must start with PSI 3 to do so, and any Psiad can learn QK.<br /> <br /> #3) As #1 or #2, but you can freely choose your 2 favored Aptitudes.<br /> <br /> #4) As any of the above, but when you go to Tier 3, all Modes can be raised to 4, not just those of your favored Aptitudes.<br /> <br /> When looking at the bonuses for combining psionic aptitudes, I'm leaning towards having them count as both of their favored aptitudes for all allies they link with, but I could use some feedback here too.<br /> <br /> I'm also wondering what sorts of things you feel might be appropriate to have as prerequisites to attaining Tier 3. (Besides PSI 6, that one is a given)<br /> <br /> I am hoping to capture the feel of the &quot;generalist&quot; Psiad to the &quot;focused&quot; Psions.<br /> <br /> I would appreciate your thoughts on which one of my ideas you would enjoy having in your game if you SG, or prefer playing as a character, if any, and why.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:27:25-08:00","id":1189132,"title":"","content":"I like the option to freely choose your two Favored Modes... Telepath / Telekinetics have always been my cup of tea : )<br /> <br /> For Tier 3 I would say:<br /> 1) Psi 6<br /> 2) A 4 in one of each of your Favored Mode's aptitudes.<br /> 3) A 3 in an Aux Mode Aptitude<br /> <br /> As far as combining for effect I would be tempted to say he can choose between serving as a factor for either of his Favored Modes (choose at the time), or paying 2 psi per use to sub in as a type of Psion in any power you have at least a dot in. Just to play up the Jack of all trades aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:37:13-08:00","id":1189134,"title":"","content":"Limited to what I can contribute, as psiad rules are a stretch goal and I hope we get there.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d suggest #1 at the moment - though the 1e and 2e rules are an imperfect mesh, you\u2019ve got a 1e framework to draw upon, and answer questions when they arise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:47:14-08:00","id":1189138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189134#post1189134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limited to what I can contribute, as psiad rules are a stretch goal and I hope we get there.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d suggest #1 at the moment - though the 1e and 2e rules are an imperfect mesh, you\u2019ve got a 1e framework to draw upon, and answer questions when they arise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue I have with #1 is that we know for a fact that in 2e Aeon, some people, heck some Psions, have/had latent Aptitude for TP/QK, and if such a person were to become a Psiad, then that would only make sense for that to be/be one of, their Favored Aptitudes. And I strongly feel that the reason the the rules in the Aberrant Players handbook disallowed QK is because the damn thing was never printed in 1e. You can come up with any excuse you'd like, but at the end of the day, it's pretty hard to favor something that never hit print.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T23:55:46-08:00","id":1189140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189132#post1189132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the option to freely choose your two Favored Modes... Telepath / Telekinetics have always been my cup of tea : )</div> </div> </div> </div>I can respect that. My personal favorite pairing is QK/PK.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189132#post1189132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Tier 3 I would say:<br /> 1) Psi 6<br /> 2) A 4 in one of each of your Favored Mode's aptitudes.<br /> 3) A 3 in an Aux Mode Aptitude</div> </div> </div> </div>According to all of my options, Mode 4 is impossible until after Tier 3, therefore it can not be a requirement to get there, but if it were to be lowered to 3 in one Mode per favored Aptitude, and 3 in a Mode of one of your secondary aptitudes... that could work...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189132#post1189132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as combining for effect I would be tempted to say he can choose between serving as a factor for either of his Favored Modes (choose at the time), or paying 2 psi per use to sub in as a type of Psion in any power you have at least a dot in. Just to play up the Jack of all trades aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that they should still be limited to favored, but I like the idea of choosing between their favored options, perhaps with the option to switch which one they are representing for 1 additional psi... thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T01:02:14-08:00","id":1189147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189138#post1189138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue I have with #1 is that we know for a fact that in 2e Aeon, some people, heck some Psions, have/had latent Aptitude for TP/QK, and if such a person were to become a Psiad, then that would only make sense for that to be/be one of, their Favored Aptitudes. And I strongly feel that the reason the the rules in the Aberrant Players handbook disallowed QK is because the damn thing was never printed in 1e. You can come up with any excuse you'd like, but at the end of the day, it's pretty hard to favor something that never hit print.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with your logic, because latents are not psiads and never will be. Psiads are not latents, and never will be. You can do what you want at your table, of course, but there\u2019s no evolutionary need for psiads to ever \u2018hold out\u2019 to Psi 3 just to have a TK/QK combination, or something with those. As far as nature is concerned, psiads have time to develop the simpler Aptitudes, and will one day grow into the more complex, higher power Aptitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:07:09-08:00","id":1189155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189147#post1189147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with your logic, because latents are not psiads</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where you are correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189147#post1189147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and never will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here is where you are wrong. All Psiads were once Latents, by definition they must be. There is no Psiad gene that is somehow different then the gene that allows one to potentially become a Psion. They are one and the same. Now, just because one is a latent does not mean that one will become a Psiad, any more then it means that you will become a Psion. Something else needs to happen to trigger you. The 1e Aberrant Players Handbook goes into this a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189147#post1189147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psiads are not latents, and never will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have the wrong order of operations. Psiads are no longer Latents, but by definition, before they manifested, they must have been, else they could not have become PSI active, which they are, and were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189147#post1189147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can do what you want at your table, of course, but there\u2019s no evolutionary need for psiads to ever \u2018hold out\u2019 to Psi 3 just to have a TK/QK combination, or something with those. As far as nature is concerned, psiads have time to develop the simpler Aptitudes, and will one day grow into the more complex, higher power Aptitudes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no holding out involved with Psiads any more then there is with Psions requiring strong latency and PSI 3 for Aptitude or Aux access to QK/TP. It's simply parity for game balance sake.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:25:44-08:00","id":1189160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189155#post1189155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is where you are correct.<br /> <br /> And here is where you are wrong. All Psiads were once Latents, by definition they must be. There is no Psiad gene that is somehow different then the gene that allows one to potentially become a Psion. They are one and the same. Now, just because one is a latent does not mean that one will become a Psiad, any more then it means that you will become a Psion. Something else needs to happen to trigger you. The 1e Aberrant Players Handbook goes into this a bit.<br /> <br /> You have the wrong order of operations. Psiads are no longer Latents, but by definition, before they manifested, they must have been, else they could not have become PSI active, which they are, and were.<br /> <br /> There is no holding out involved with Psiads any more then there is with Psions requiring strong latency and PSI 3 for Aptitude or Aux access to QK/TP. It's simply parity for game balance sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that you are disagreeing with one of the authors of \u00c6on 2nd edition, right? In the event we do get psiad rules for \u00c6on, his opinion on the matter is far more likely to be taken into account, assuming Bunyip is not the one <b><i>writing those rules</i></b>. I imagine that he is not wrong; it is far more likely psiads arise from latent parents and could not be 'activated' by a Prometheus chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:31:20-08:00","id":1189165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189160#post1189160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that you are disagreeing with one of the authors of \u00c6on 2nd edition, right? In the event we do get psiad rules for \u00c6on, his opinion on the matter is far more likely to be taken into account, assuming Bunyip is not the one <b><i>writing those rules</i></b>. I imagine that he is not wrong; it is far more likely psiads arise from latent parents and could not be 'activated' by a Prometheus chamber.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is still human, and has been wrong before. What he chooses to write in the future is on him, but as of right now, Psiads only exist in 1e, and going by everything in 1e I am right, and I can give page #'s to prove it. And besides, that just means that changing his mind now, while the rules are unwritten is far more important then convincing him after they are in print.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:44:47-08:00","id":1189181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189155#post1189155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is where you are correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt; Snipping from here mostly for comedy\u2019s sake &gt;<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll agree to disagree, and that\u2019s fine. I heartily endorse what works for your table. Once day soon (Setting Secrets chapter) we\u2019ll be able to dig into why I\u2019m arguing as I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:48:36-08:00","id":1189183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189160#post1189160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that you are disagreeing with one of the authors of \u00c6on 2nd edition, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey FallenEco, I appreciate the sentiment, but I\u2019m as open to debate and change as anyone. I have my opinions, but until words are put on a page, nothing is set in stone. Besides, regardless of what my opinion is, the developer (John) might disagree, and I\u2019ll write to the brief, since I like getting paid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In other words, let\u2019s enjoy the debate and see where it takes us.<br /> <br /> That said, sadly I\u2019ll probably have to stop about here, as I do want to write the rules one day. That doesn\u2019t mean you all should stop - I\u2019ll be reading along, and may chip in for clarity if asked or needed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:52:46-08:00","id":1189184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189181#post1189181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt; Snipping from here mostly for comedy\u2019s sake &gt;<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll agree to disagree, and that\u2019s fine. I heartily endorse what works for your table. Once day soon (Setting Secrets chapter) we\u2019ll be able to dig into why I\u2019m arguing as I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I only have the First Edition Aberrant Players Guide to work with, and to call those rules lacking, and incomplete is being generous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T08:13:07-08:00","id":1189229,"title":"","content":"I would choose options 3 and 4, mostly because I see flexibility and open options to be a very very very good thing. So if a person wants to combine TP and VK then they should be able to. <br /> <br /> To be honest when I read th Psiad idea / rules my mind came up with more ideas then the limited nature of the one aptitude only Psion. (Which I only don't super dislike as there is actually a setting was in for the restriction,so it's entertaining). <br /> <br /> I also think it would be cool for Psions to be able break down the artificial genetic barrier and become a Psiad, getting access to more Aptitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T09:50:53-08:00","id":1189249,"title":"","content":"After scaning the first post, #4) appeals to me. Psiads need some way to blend with psions so that a new type with psion power and psiad flexibility could rise. Psicog, psi plus cognition slash awareness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T10:49:16-08:00","id":1189261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189147#post1189147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree with your logic, because latents are not psiads and never will be. Psiads are not latents, and never will be. You can do what you want at your table, of course, but there\u2019s no evolutionary need for psiads to ever \u2018hold out\u2019 to Psi 3 just to have a TK/QK combination, or something with those. As far as nature is concerned, psiads have time to develop the simpler Aptitudes, and will one day grow into the more complex, higher power Aptitudes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so, I'm not going to say &quot;you're wrong&quot; because that's stupid and it's literally you writing this game.<br /> <br /> What I am going to say is &quot;Please explain, because the word <i>latent</i> has a specific meaning and a psiad that hasn't awakened to his powers yet would absolutely conform to that meaning.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T23:29:45-08:00","id":1189355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189261#post1189261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so, I'm not going to say &quot;you're wrong&quot; because that's stupid and it's literally you writing this game.<br /> <br /> What I am going to say is &quot;Please explain, because the word <i>latent</i> has a specific meaning and a psiad that hasn't awakened to his powers yet would absolutely conform to that meaning.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, What?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As mentioned maybe something along the lines of two latents can have a Psiad child at a rare rate. Or maybe Psiads are something else and and aren't connected to the Latent/Psion as closely as assumed. I say be patient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T01:37:56-08:00","id":1189366,"title":"","content":"Maybe the latents are just what the Doyen called those humans particularly susceptible to their biotech genetic manipulation that turns humans into psions as part of their deception of the Proxies.<br /> <br /> Actual latent Psiads are something else entirely, likely even more elusive and undocumented than Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T03:27:02-08:00","id":1189375,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been trying to think of a succinct way of explaining it without getting bogged down in too much detail.<br /> <br /> A latent is what happens when you have a human with the potential to develop psionic power, but who has no outlet for that power. The potential builds to an extent, but eventually stops. It\u2019s an evolutionary dead end (psionically), but someone has given humanity hacks to get around it.<br /> <br /> A psiad is what happens when you have a human with the potential to develop psionic power, *and* the means to express that power. As the power builds, they learn to express it. They don\u2019t become latents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T04:09:21-08:00","id":1189382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189375#post1189375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been trying to think of a succinct way of explaining it without getting bogged down in too much detail.<br /> <br /> A latent is what happens when you have a human with the potential to develop psionic power, but who has no outlet for that power. The potential builds to an extent, but eventually stops. It\u2019s an evolutionary dead end (psionically), but someone has given humanity hacks to get around it.<br /> <br /> A psiad is what happens when you have a human with the potential to develop psionic power, *and* the means to express that power. As the power builds, they learn to express it. They don\u2019t become latents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... very different then what they were in 1e... and I'll be honest... I'm not sure if I like the change or not. I'm going to need to think about this for a bit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T04:28:12-08:00","id":1189383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189382#post1189382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... very different then what they were in 1e</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. All I\u2019ve done is explain why I\u2019m differentiating between latents and psiads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189382#post1189382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and I'll be honest... I'm not sure if I like the change or not. I'm going to need to think about this for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely up to you. Unless the pace of the Kickstarter takes off in the final few days, we won\u2019t be seeing any official rules for psiads for quite a while, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T06:18:05-08:00","id":1189390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189382#post1189382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... very different then what they were in 1e... and I'll be honest... I'm not sure if I like the change or not. I'm going to need to think about this for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC the only thing that 1st Edition had to say on the matter was the following text, from the APG, p. 58: <i>A nova doesn't develop psi talent; he grows an M-R node. Conversely, a psych won't develop a node; he possesses latency, which may later develop into psychic power.</i><br /> <br /> That definitely implies that you first become a latent, and can then become either a psion or a psiad. However, just like Trinity 1e used Taint interchangeably for the two traits Aberrant 1e called Taint and Quantum, any discussion of psychic capability in an Aberrant book should be taken with a grain of salt. In the context of Aberrant, the details are irrelevant.<br /> <br /> So <i>technically </i>it's a change from how it was presented in 1e, but it's not what I would personally call &quot;very different.&quot; We're just tweaking the terminology a bit.<br /> <br /> This is hardly the first change we've made from 1e (just wait until you see the Setting Secrets chapter), and it certainly won't be the last. But, as we keep pointing out, this is a continuum: if you don't like our answer, you can use your own, and that's fine by us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:03:27-08:00","id":1189399,"title":"","content":"Besides, the Aeon Companion, are there any other Aeon (not basic Trinity, Aberrant or Adventure!) books on the schedule, or if not approved, do you have any idea of a supplement order?<br /> <br /> If psiads don't make it as a stretch goal, which sadly appears likely, when might we see them and in what context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:09:04-08:00","id":1189400,"title":"","content":"Hmm. This is all very intriguing. And makes me wish that Psiad rules were more close to coming or you guys had already created them because you realized people would want them. <br /> <br /> Buuuut considering how well done both the Continuum Core and the Aeon Rulebook are you guys have some trust leeway with me. So I'll wait and see before passing judgement. <br /> <br /> I really want Psiads as I hate the fact that the main group of powers in Trinity are alien created and limited and want to play the natural psychics. <br /> <br /> Though I'm with the group thst puts Psiads as latents till they manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:28:09-08:00","id":1189404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189382#post1189382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... very different then what they were in 1e... and I'll be honest... I'm not sure if I like the change or not. I'm going to need to think about this for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a nuanced change, but not a significantly different one, and I can see how it could work conceptually.<br /> <br /> Here's a (possibly terrible) analogy: think of a chicken egg.<br /> <br /> The Psaid chicken egg matures, grows, and eventually the chick inside gains some sense of mobility and awareness. At that point, it breaks the shell and becomes a Psiad Chick. It's young, it's weak, but it has the potential to some day slowly grow to become a Psiad Chicken.<br /> <br /> The Psion chicken egg also matures, grows, and gains some sense of mobility and awareness. However, on its own it lacks the strength to break the shell. So there's a chick inside, but it'll never develop, or grow, or erupt on its own. It might occasionally wiggle around; maybe it even learns to roll a little. But that's it. It is, then, a <i>Latent Chicken</i>.<br /> <br /> What the Doyen did was find all of those Latent Chickens, and give them a dose of Psi-Chicken Gene Therapy. (PCGT; powerful stuff!) That genetic bump force-grew their legs, their wings, and effectively *punched* them out of the shell. The resulting freaky chicken is a Psion.<br /> <br /> The reason why starting Psions have stronger powers, potential, and even Psi than Psiad is that the PCGT specifically works like Psi steroids; it bulks up their abilities and powers, at the cost of, uh, &quot;shriveling&quot; some other very important things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12757-dao-jones","name":"Dao Jones","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T08:37:32-08:00","id":1189408,"title":"","content":"Interesting theory.<br /> <br /> Now, more importantly, why the did the Psi Chicken cross the road? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T09:09:37-08:00","id":1189415,"title":"","content":"Going back to the original post, I'm considering the possibility of a fifth option: Psiads resemble Mesmerists more than they do Psions. That is, Psiads pick up individual psi powers in a haphazard manner that's more like how Talents select their Gifts than how Psions put dots into Modes: you can, say, pick up Sensory Manipulation without having to pick up Orientation or Dowsing first. <br /> <br /> During character creation, a psiad gets more dots to spend on powers than a psion does (say, ten instead of four); but the powers are more expensive: it takes one more dot than the power's rating to pick it up. So a basic power costs one dot, a one-dot power costs two dots, a two-dot power costs three dots, and a three-dot power costs four dots.<br /> <br /> While the Prometheus Chamber amplifies a psion's power, it also structures and restricts it, limiting the psion to the Modes of one Aptitude but allowing him to advance beyond three dots within those Modes. Psiads don't have that restriction, and his choices aren't limited to what Modes provide. <span style=\"color:gray\">[This is to allow for the importing of Psychic Knacks from <b>Adventure!</b> that don't match up with any of the powers available to psions.]</span> Their choices aren't <i>totally</i> unfettered, though: you still need Psi 3+ in order to pick up Quantakinetic or Teleport powers, and there may be further restrictions on which Aptitudes are readily available to the psiad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:36:39-08:00","id":1189444,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> - Thanks, for putting more detail around my quick words before I headed off for the night.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar258_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"258\" data-vbnamecard=\"258\">TheSarcasticSage</a> - I find it slightly amusing that you\u2019re saying \u2018this is different from 1e\u2019, when (a) I suggested in post #3 that you stick close to 1e rules, and you argued against it, and (b) 1e rules clearly state that Quantakinesis is 100% out of bounds, your character cannot have it, and changing that is one of the goals you\u2019re most keen to pursue.<br /> <br /> For everyone - I\u2019ve read what came before in the APG, and about Mesmerists in Adventure! (And all of the Trinity line, piecing together the different hints and clues about how psionic potential works.) There are some interesting ideas going on in this thread, and nothing is set in stone yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T13:46:07-08:00","id":1189456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dao Jones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189404#post1189404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a nuanced change, but not a significantly different one, and I can see how it could work conceptually.<br /> <br /> Here's a (possibly terrible) analogy: think of a chicken egg.<br /> <br /> The Psaid chicken egg matures, grows, and eventually the chick inside gains some sense of mobility and awareness. At that point, it breaks the shell and becomes a Psiad Chick. It's young, it's weak, but it has the potential to some day slowly grow to become a Psiad Chicken.<br /> <br /> The Psion chicken egg also matures, grows, and gains some sense of mobility and awareness. However, on its own it lacks the strength to break the shell. So there's a chick inside, but it'll never develop, or grow, or erupt on its own. It might occasionally wiggle around; maybe it even learns to roll a little. But that's it. It is, then, a <i>Latent Chicken</i>.<br /> <br /> What the Doyen did was find all of those Latent Chickens, and give them a dose of Psi-Chicken Gene Therapy. (PCGT; powerful stuff!) That genetic bump force-grew their legs, their wings, and effectively *punched* them out of the shell. The resulting freaky chicken is a Psion.<br /> <br /> The reason why starting Psions have stronger powers, potential, and even Psi than Psiad is that the PCGT specifically works like Psi steroids; it bulks up their abilities and powers, at the cost of, uh, &amp;quot;shriveling&amp;quot; some other very important things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad analogy, and basically what I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T16:24:02-08:00","id":1189490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189456#post1189456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a bad analogy, and basically what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, lets take a moment and go with the egg analogy. An unfertilized egg would be a Baseline or Talent. They will never be a Chicken (PSI/Quantum Active). A fertilized egg has 2 possibilities, Viable genetics lead to an eventual hatching (Eruption event) that produces chickens (Psiad/Nova), non-viable leads to stillborn unhatched eggs (Latent). The things that breaks the analogy, are 1) Without an Eruption Event, perfectly viable &quot;Eggs&quot; to use this example, will never reach their potential &quot;active&quot; selves, 2) Until Eruption, both viable, and non-viable fertilized &quot;eggs&quot; will show as Latent to testing, because until they erupt, by definition, they are latent. It's what they word means... &quot;lying dormant or hidden until circumstances are suitable for development or manifestation.&quot; 3) Significant exposure to PSI/Quantum energies can and do trigger &quot;Latents&quot; into becoming full fledged members of the energy type (Psiad/Nova). Therefore there really is no such thing as non-viable fertilized eggs in this example, there are just some that require more &quot;oomph&quot; to trigger then others. However I agree that right now in Aeon, some peoples potential may be so miniscule that they require spiritual castration (Prometheus Chamber) to trigger (Psions), but, in theory, if the circumstances were right (Eruption Event), including &quot;enough&quot; of the right energy (PSI/Quantum) with the right (PSI/Quantum) genetic marker, anyone could trigger and go full active.<br /> <br /> tl:dr - In 1e, the Nova/PSI genetic markers were the exact same until triggered, and in order to get a full Nova/Psiad, all you needed were 1) the right genetic marker (ie. Latency), 2) &quot;Enough&quot; residual energy of the &quot;correct&quot; type (PSI/Quantum), 3) A triggering event, and you get yourself a new Nova/Psiad. If you are missing #1 you are a baseline or Talent, if you are missing either #' 2 and/or 3, then you are a latent.<br /> <br /> The fact that you are basically saying that &quot;this is not the case&quot; isn't making any sense to me, and that is why it doesn't sit well with me.<br /> <br /> I know changes happen between editions, and I can do whatever I want at my table, but I'm hoping that the Settings Secrets chapter will help explain what changes have been made, and then you can talk about why those changes were made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T23:14:09-08:00","id":1189536,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re right, it\u2019s not a perfect analogy, and it\u2019s full of holes. I haven\u2019t managed to think of a perfect analogy yet.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m saying is that although the APG presented a very Aberrant-centric view of the world, and said \u2018you can basically use this for psiads as well\u2019, there\u2019s no actual requirement that psiads experience an \u2018eruption event\u2019. That\u2019s just because things were written trough an Aberrant game line lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T00:11:56-08:00","id":1189546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189536#post1189536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019re right, it\u2019s not a perfect analogy, and it\u2019s full of holes. I haven\u2019t managed to think of a perfect analogy yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>There never is, but this one was particularly flawed, and people were starting to act like it was a perfect response, so I felt I need to point out why it was... imperfect at best...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189536#post1189536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I\u2019m saying is that although the APG presented a very Aberrant-centric view of the world, and said \u2018you can basically use this for psiads as well\u2019, there\u2019s no actual requirement that psiads experience an \u2018eruption event\u2019. That\u2019s just because things were written trough an Aberrant game line lens.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't Aberrant only phenomenon. Every game line, Adventure! and Trinity included, had transformative moments, and still do. In this new edition Talents still have a &quot;Moment of Inspiration&quot;, Psions have their time in the tanks, Novas Erupt, Psiads are no different. Even Psions going to from Tier 2-3 is described as follows &quot;Psions normally experience this change as a profound transformation that can include visions, sudden bursts of knowledge, and a general feeling of awakening and increased awareness over the next day or two.&quot;<br /> <br /> Call it an awakening instead of eruption if you want, but everyone has them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T02:07:09-08:00","id":1189559,"title":"","content":"Based on 1e, as far as I can recall, anyway, Nova children of Novas didn't Erupt. They were born with a distributed MR Node, power that came quite naturally to them, and little or no trouble with Taint.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T03:31:11-08:00","id":1189568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189546#post1189546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In this new edition Talents still have a &quot;Moment of Inspiration&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trinity Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A subtle transformation, so integrated into the life of the Talent that even she does not consciously know what happened, or what she does to access it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a moment that (noticeably) separates psiad from baseline. That\u2019s the moment that her Psi grows from 1 to 2. I\u2019ve never claimed any different. What I\u2019ve said is that if that person didn\u2019t have the right stuff to become a psiad, that moment would simply change her from baseline to latent. Psiads don\u2019t come from latents because when their psi has developed enough to flow, it flows. Latents don\u2019t become psiads because their psi can\u2019t flow. They need someone to construct a channel for it to flow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1189126-homebrew-psiads?p=1189546#post1189546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call it an awakening instead of eruption if you want, but everyone has them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. But maybe not. (As nikink noted with 2nd generation novas.)<br /> <br /> Look, all this is irrelevant to whatever home brew psiad rules will work for you anyway. So I\u2019m going to drop this aspect of the conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-26-2018, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T22:52:23-08:00","id":1190574,"title":"","content":"Amazing! Looks like we made it to psiads. You\u2019ll be seeing them sooner rather than later. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m incredibly excited!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T05:05:34-08:00","id":1190619,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I'm kinda hoping we have such a last-few-hours surge that we pile on past even the current stretch goals, but it's great that we're getting psiads already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:21:17-08:00","id":1191654,"title":"","content":"Well we is it, we got Psiads now we have to wait to see what they come up with. <br /> <br /> I basically want Psiads to be able to learn all Aptitudes at say 3, proxy tier maybe 5, and above proxy tier 7 or higher. I do not want teleportation or quantickenetics banned, that's not fun. <br /> <br /> I so do not want thst paired aptitude thing from Aberrant. Psiads should not be so grouped, they should be free to learn as they wish. <br /> <br /> I think cost in exp could be higher, to represent difficulty in such spread out power gain. <br /> <br /> One of the things I liked and will add is that Psiads are immune to Doyen psychic possession unless they have been directed manipulated like the proxies were. <br /> <br /> The thing is that they have the potential to be more powerful but it's harder and takes longer and that's the balancing factor. That and super rarity, they are very very uncommon, maybe a few hundred in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}